  "id": "link-game",
  "description": "Linking a game identity after a regular sign-in (WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.11.4, §12.11.7). A Game Center exchange found no link and answered a link handle. The person signs in on this device through the browser, which leaves a step-up of 300 s. GET link names the kinds the person could add: a game kind always carries reach developer, known before any token. POST link with the handle and a pkey-proof/1 link proof adds the Game Center identity under the developer's team. A later sign-in earns a new step-up. Play Games has no handle in this conversation: POST link carries the server auth code as subjectToken with subjectTokenType urn:polaris-key:token-type:pgs-server-auth-code, a nonce, the device's keys and a proof over the nonce, the key and the token's hash. The Worker redeems the code and adds the Play Games identity under the product's application. Each link spends the step-up, so the offer drops the kind that was added.",
